free_entry['title']='Candidate two-atom refutation of eventual free log-unimodality for a>arcosh(2)'
free_entry['statement']+=' For nu=(delta_(exp(-a))+delta_(exp(a)))/2 and sigma_t the free positive multiplicative Brownian law in Hasebe-Ueda-Wang, arXiv:2009.13848, the exact Lemma 4.1(3) criterion therefore implies sigma_t free-multiplicatively convolved with nu is not log-unimodal for every t>=T. This is a candidate refutation awaiting the independent auditor; novelty is unverified.'
free_entry['proof_text']+=' The cached primary Lemma 4.1(3) equates log-unimodality to at most two positive r-roots of (sin R/R) integral r xi/(1+r^2 xi^2-2r xi cos R) dnu(xi)=1/t for every R in (0,pi). For the two reciprocal atoms substitute r=exp(u); the integral is F_R(u). Its four roots violate this necessary condition. The primary normalization was checked locally in source_check_receipt.json; independent proof review is still pending.'
free_entry['kind']='theorem'
by_key['odd-dimensional-ideal-hole-positive-beta-polynomial']['statement']=PREFIX+"For m>=1 define I(q)=integral over R^(2m) of [sqrt((q+1)^2/4+|z|^2)-(q-1)/2]^(-4m) dz and H(u)=I(1)exp(-2mu)/I(exp(2u)). Then 1/H(u)=exp(2mu)p_m(exp(2u)), where p_m is a degree-m polynomial with positive rational coefficients and p_m(1)=1. Explicitly p_m(q)=(2/B(m,m))sum_(k=0)^m A_k q^k, with A_k=binom(m-1,k)[B(2m+k,m)-B(2m+k+1,m)/2]+binom(m-1,k-1)B(2m+k,m)/2, where B(a,b)=(a-1)!(b-1)!/(a+b-1)! and out-of-range binomial coefficients are zero."
by_key['dimension-two-ideal-hole-negative-sixth-coefficient']['statement']=PREFIX+"Define H_2(u)=pi/[4 cosh(u)^2 arctan(exp(u))+2 sinh(u)] near u=0. For f(u)=exp(-u)/H_2(u), the sixth Maclaurin coefficient is 61/240-4/(5pi)<-1/2640<0. Thus these coefficients are not all positive in u. This H_2 is obtained by evaluating the n=1 normalized ideal-hole integral in P0411_PROOF.md; the coefficient claim itself concerns the explicitly defined function."
by_key['wired-largest-cluster-inherits-boundary-surface-limit']['statement']=PREFIX+"For iid nearest-neighbor bond percolation on Z^d, d>3, assume full-space tails P(0 connects to l_infinity distance >=r)<=K/(r+1)^gamma, gamma>1, and P(|C(0)|>=k)<=K_2 k^(-1/2). In B_n={0,...,n-1}^d identify all vertex-boundary points, without changing internal Bernoulli edges, and count components in original vertices. Then |C_max^(wired)|/n^(d-1)->2d sum_(r>=0)q_r in probability, where q_r is the probability that (r,0,...,0) connects to {x_1=0} within {x_1>=0}. The largest component not touching the boundary is o_P(n^(d-1))."
for result in results:
    key=result['id'][len('w334-'):]
